<Layout title="Support · Lovepins" description="Lovepins help and contact: pairing, photos, subscription, cancelling, and deleting your account." path="/support/">
<article class="prose wrap">
  <h1>Help &amp; support</h1>
  <p class="muted">Lovepins: your love story, on one map.</p>
<h2>Support</h2>
  <div class="card">
    <p>Need help, found a bug, or have an idea? Email us at <a href="mailto:hello@lovepins.app">hello@lovepins.app</a>. We usually answer within two business days.</p>
  </div>

  <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>

  <h3>How do I pair with my partner?</h3>
  <p>One of you taps <em>Invite my partner</em> and shares the 6-character code. The other taps <em>I have a code</em> and enters it. You then share the same map.</p>

  <h3>Can my partner see my photos?</h3>
  <p>Not yet. Photos stay on the iPhone that added them. Your partner sees your pins, ratings and notes, but not your photos.</p>

  <h3>Does one subscription cover both of us?</h3>
  <p>Yes. Lovepins Premium is shared by the couple: one of you subscribes, both of you get it.</p>

  <h3>How do I cancel my subscription?</h3>
  <p>Subscriptions are managed by Apple: Settings › Apple ID › Subscriptions › Lovepins. You can also tap <em>Manage subscription</em> in the app (<em>Us</em> tab).</p>

  <h3 id="password">I forgot my password</h3>
  <p>We can't reset passwords by email yet. If you signed up with Apple or Google, use that button on the sign-in screen. Otherwise, email <a href="mailto:hello@lovepins.app">hello@lovepins.app</a> from the address you signed up with and we'll help you get back in.</p>

  <h3>Do we both need the app?</h3>
  <p>To share a map, yes, but you don't have to start together. Tap <em>Start on my own</em>, pin your dates, and invite your partner later from the <em>Us</em> tab. Everything you pinned comes along.</p>

  <h3>How do I leave a couple or delete my account?</h3>
  <p>Open the <em>Us</em> tab › <em>Leave our couple</em> or <em>Delete my account</em>. See the <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> for what happens to your data.</p>

  
</article>
</Layout>
